course: dictionary
lesson: 9110
title: Smear and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Smear is a good example. «Some farmers smear fences with chilli and grease» means they spread something sticky or oily over the fences. The sentence is about fences and grease, so smear is about spreading, not about a dirty mark.
explain: Smear can also be a noun, meaning a mark. If you find a smear of jam on the window, that is a dirty mark where something was rubbed. Smear can mean to blur a mark, as when ink smudges across a page, or to spread false stories to hurt someone, as in a «smear campaign».
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around smear. Ask what is being smeared and why. If the words are about fences, grease and chilli, it is about spreading. If the words are about lies and a damaged reputation, it is about unfair attacks. Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Smear is a verb (smear, smears, smeared, smearing) and a noun (a smear, smears).
fact: «Smear» means to spread something soft, sticky or oily over a surface, often messily.
fact: A smear can also be a dirty mark made by something rubbed on a surface.
fact: «A smear campaign» means spreading false or unfair stories to damage someone's good name.
fact: «Some farmers smear fences with chilli and grease», because chilli stings elephants' sensitive trunks.
exercise: «Some farmers smear fences with chilli and grease.» What does smear mean here? | Wash something clean with water | Count how many fences there are | Cut wood into thin planks | *To spread something sticky or oily over a surface
exercise: Ella finds a smear of jam on the window. What is a smear here? | A bright, shiny sticker | *A dirty mark made by something rubbed on a surface | A tidy row of little dots
exercise: «They ran a smear campaign to damage the mayor's good name.» What is a smear campaign? | A plan to paint the school fence | A campaign to clean up the town streets | A game with lots of rules | *Spreading false or unfair stories to hurt someone
test: Maya's pen leaked, and she smeared the ink across the page as she wrote. What does smeared mean here? | Folded the page in half | *Rubbed so the ink blurred and spread | Drew a neat straight line | Dried quickly in the sun
test: «Some farmers smear fences with chilli and grease», so what is being spread? | Water and soap | Paint and glitter | *Chilli and grease
exam: Which word shows that smearing happened yesterday? | *smeared | smears | smearing
